## 27. Product-Level Cost Calculation

Create a product profitability calculator.

For each watch, calculate:

Landed Cost per Unit =
Purchase Price
+ Applicable Inbound Freight
+ Import/Duty Costs, if applicable
+ Quality Inspection Cost
+ Allocated Packaging Cost
+ Other Direct Procurement Costs.

Maintain the tax treatment separately according to accounting and GST configuration. Do not treat recoverable input tax as a business expense without proper accounting treatment.

Calculate:

Gross Profit = Net Product Revenue - Cost of Goods Sold.

Gross Margin Percentage = Gross Profit / Net Product Revenue × 100.

Contribution Margin =
Net Revenue
- Cost of Goods Sold
- Variable Payment Fees
- Variable Shipping Costs
- Packaging Costs
- Discounts
- Expected Variable Return/RTO Costs
- Variable Marketing Costs.

Clearly define the components to prevent double counting.

Display the result for each watch SKU.

